Copyright (c) 2026 The authors of HU-OCR. All rights reserved.

Applies to all versions published on or after 9 October 2026. Earlier
versions were published under the MIT License; those already published
versions remain under that license.

1. Permitted use
   The software "HU-OCR" (scripts, user interface, documentation, graphics)
   may be downloaded, installed and run free of charge - by private
   individuals, schools, public authorities, associations and companies.
   Copies for your own use (e.g. on USB drives, servers or shares of your
   own organization) are permitted.

2. Own settings
   Adjusting the configuration file (config.json), the folders, the naming
   rules and the download URLs with a text editor or the included tools
   (Config-OCR, Rules-OCR) is expressly permitted.

3. Not permitted (without prior written consent of the authors)
   a) to modify, adapt or translate the scripts or the documentation, or to
      incorporate any part of them into other software,
   b) to use or distribute modified versions,
   c) to sell or rent the software, or to offer it for a fee as part of a
      product or service,
   d) to publish the software outside the official repository
      (distribution within your own organization is permitted),
   e) to remove or alter copyright, license or version notices.

4. Third-party software
   This license applies ONLY to the scripts and documentation in this
   repository. It does NOT cover the third-party tools that are downloaded
   on first run directly from their official sources into the local bin\
   folder (Python, Tesseract, Ghostscript, qpdf, ocrmypdf, 7-Zip, etc.).
   Those are governed solely by their own licenses, which the user accepts
   by downloading and using them. See NOTICE.md for details.

5. GitHub
   Viewing and forking the repository within the GitHub Terms of Service
   remains unaffected. A fork does not grant any of the rights listed
   under section 3.

6. Warranty and liability
   The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. To the
   extent permitted by law, the authors are not liable for any damage,
   data loss or consequential damage arising from its use. OCR results and
   automatically generated file names must be checked before further use.

7. Final provisions
   This license is governed by Austrian law. Should any provision be
   invalid, the remaining provisions shall remain in effect.
